  origin: ?{\text{cited: the value on both chambers, with the multiplicity at Newton distance one as an upper bound, is}\ \cite[Theorem~9.1 with Propositions~9.5 and~9.6]{KamimotoNose2016}\text{, which restates}\ \cite[Theorem~0.4]{Varchenko1976}\text{; proved here: the bound from above in both chambers, with the multiplicities, and its certificate through \cref{lem:count}(above), with the prices, the combinations and the cover in closed form on the two chambers}}

